RBAC:

RBAC in Kubernetes controls access to resources using Roles/ClusterRoles and RoleBindings/ClusterRoleBindings.
A Role provides permissions within a namespace, while a ClusterRole provides permissions across the entire cluster.
RoleBinding – Grants the permissions defined in a Role to a user, group, or service account within a namespace.

ClusterRoleBinding – Grants ClusterRole permissions across the entire cluster.
_____________________________________________
apiVersion: v1
kind: ServiceAccount
metadata:
  name: devops-sa
  namespace: dev

---

apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: Role
metadata:
  name: pod-reader
  namespace: dev
rules:
- apiGroups: [""]
  resources: ["pods"]
  verbs: ["get","list","watch"]--------verbs define actions that can be performed on a resourse

---

apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: RoleBinding
metadata:
  name: pod-reader-binding
  namespace: dev
subjects:
- kind: ServiceAccount
  name: devops-sa
  namespace: dev

roleRef:
  kind: Role
  name: pod-reader
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io

---

apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRole
metadata:
  name: node-reader
rules:
- apiGroups: [""]
  resources: ["nodes"]
  verbs: ["get","list","watch"]

---

apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
kind: ClusterRoleBinding
metadata:
  name: node-reader-binding
subjects:
- kind: ServiceAccount
  name: devops-sa
  namespace: dev

roleRef:
  kind: ClusterRole
  name: node-reader
  apiGroup: rbac.authorization.k8s.io

______________________________________________________________________
| Verb                 | Action                     |
| -------------------- | -------------------------- |
| **get**              | Read a specific resource   |
| **list**             | List resources             |
| **watch**            | Monitor changes            |
| **create**           | Create new resource        |
| **update**           | Modify existing resource   |
| **patch**            | Partial update             |
| **delete**           | Delete resource            |
| **deletecollection** | Delete multiple resources  |
| **exec**             | Execute command inside pod |
| **proxy**            | Access service proxy       |





_________________________________________________________________________

What This YAML Does
1️⃣ ServiceAccount

Creates a service account called devops-sa in the dev namespace.

2️⃣ Role

Gives permission to:

get pods

list pods

watch pods

Inside dev namespace only.

3️⃣ RoleBinding

Connects the Role → ServiceAccount.

4️⃣ ClusterRole

Gives permission to read nodes at cluster level.

5️⃣ ClusterRoleBinding

Attaches ClusterRole → ServiceAccount.
